CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 4 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --graphml-witness witness.graphml
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
Invariant check failed
--
Building a counterexample is the one path --array-rf touches that no SUCCESSFUL
run ever reaches, so it needs its own test.

--array-rf replaces each `index(array, j)` in the equation with a fresh
scalar. The first version made those plain symbol_exprt, which every solver
path accepts -- but build_goto_trace asserts that what it finds in an SSA step
carries ID_C_SSA_symbol, so the run aborted in "Building error trace" with
"wrong SSA expression ID". They are ssa_exprt now.

Nothing caught it until the deployment check ran the competition wrapper, which
passes --graphml-witness: 537 earlier runs, including every expected-false task
in three families, had answered FAILED without ever building a witness. Two
tasks went from FAILED to ERROR the moment they did.

This test asks for the witness explicitly, and forbids the invariant message as
well as the wrong verdict, so a regression shows up as a failure here rather
than as an ERROR in the competition.
